<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8848" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθραξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰκος</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>charcoal,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sotad.Com.
				1.12
			</span></i>: mostly in pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθρακες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					34
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				332
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Nu.</u>
				97
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. Παρνήθιοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					348
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπτωμέναις κόγχαισιν ἐπί τῶν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					68
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθρακας ἡμμένους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.100
				</span></i>
			, etc.; their vapour produced stupor, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Sens.</u>
				444b31
			</span></i>: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθρακας
			κατεσθίειν,</span> of a glutton, <i><span class="en">
				Euphro
				10.14
			</span></i>, cf. Ion Trag.<i><span class="en">
				29
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>coal,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷς καὶ οἱ χαλκεῖς χρῶνται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Lap.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PHolm.</u>
				2.33
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ ἀνθράκων μαλακῶν</span>
			on a slow <i>fire,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Xenocr.
				16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> a precious
			stone of dark-red colour, including the <i>carbuncle, ruby,</i>
			and <i>garnet</i> (<span class="entity">Adams</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				387b18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				28.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phylarch.
				41
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> hence,
				<i>carbuncle, malignant pustule</i> (acc. to some,
				<i>small-pox</i>), <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				3.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				7.719
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσάτις</span>
			, <i>woad,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PHolm.
				18.34
			</span></i>, al.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
